diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index a54ea645..74f5bfd2 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- **Configuration baseline and drift:** record the current configuration of selected Deployments, StatefulSets, DaemonSets, Services, Ingresses, NetworkPolicies and ConfigMaps as a baseline, then run a check to see what has drifted. Each resource is reported as match, changed, missing or not checked (never silently a match), changes have a priority, and a source ("according to managedFields", "applied from Kubron") is shown only when there is evidence. Versions are immutable and created only after a preview, a comment and an explicit confirmation that the current state, including existing deviations, is recorded; exceptions (with a comment and an optional expiry) are kept separately and listed in every result. Secrets are never read, and values that may be sensitive are stored only as keyed hashes. Kubron only reads the cluster: it applies and fixes nothing and checks only on request. See `docs/baseline.md`.
+- **Baseline permission and settings:** the new `baseline.manage` permission (administrators by default) is required to create versions, change the active version, manage exceptions and delete baselines; viewing and running a check need `read`. On the server, check results are kept for 90 days (`KUBRON_BASELINE_RESULTS_RETENTION_DAYS`) and at least the 20 latest versions of each baseline are kept, the active one always (`KUBRON_BASELINE_MIN_VERSIONS`). The server stores baselines in PostgreSQL (migration `0013_baselines`), with version content encrypted and included in key rotation.
+
 ## [1.2.1] - 2026-11-10
 
 ### Added
